{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta User Session Impersonation",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Defense Evasion / T1550\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta User Session Impersonation\" or \"<ip>|Okta User Session Impersonation\"\n\nA user has initiated a session impersonation granting them access to the environment with the permissions of the user they are impersonating. This would likely indicate Okta administrative access and should only ever occur if requested and expected.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_user_impersonation_access/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_user_impersonation_access.toml",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "detection",
    "authentication-sessions",
    "defense-evasion",
    "T1550"
  ],
  "Schedule": "10,25,40,55 * * * *",
